# 5. PREFERRED CRYPTOGRAPHIC ARCHITECTURE

Biometric unlock must not merely authenticate the user.

It must also securely recover the same existing Aman Rayan master vault key.

Use:

# WebAuthn PRF Extension

when supported.

The PRF output associated with the WebAuthn credential must be used to derive a client-side key capable of decrypting a second wrapped copy of the existing master vault key.

Architecture:

```text
Existing PIN route:

PIN
↓
PBKDF2-derived key
↓
decrypt PIN-wrapped master key
↓
Master Vault Key


New biometric route:

WebAuthn credential
↓
user verification
↓
PRF output
↓
derived biometric wrapping key
↓
decrypt biometric-wrapped master key
↓
Same Master Vault Key
```

There must still be ONLY ONE logical vault master key.

Do not create a second vault encryption system.

